{
  title: "239 a binding used in a constructor is shared across reads"
  doc: "eu-oaz72.40: a binding referred to once inside a block field or list
        element can be read any number of times through the structure, so
        demand analysis must not mark it AtMostOnce (which skips its update
        frame). The tick gate is in `tests/harness_test.rs`, which runs these
        targets with demand analysis on and requires each three-read target
        to cost about one fold."
}

` "the target computes the right value"
passes(context): (context.result.ok) then(:PASS, :FAIL)

p(n): { m: range(0, n) foldl(+, 0) }.([m])
h(n): { m: range(0, n) foldl(+, 0)  l: [m] }.l

` { target: :fold
    verify: [:passes] }
fold: {
  ok: (range(0, 20000) foldl(+, 0)) = 199990000
}

# A list literal as a block's body: three reads, one fold if shared.
` { target: :list-body
    verify: [:passes] }
list-body: {
  x: p(20000)
  y: [x first, x first, x first]
  ok: y = [199990000, 199990000, 199990000]
}

# A list held in a selected block field: three reads, one fold if shared.
` { target: :list-field
    verify: [:passes] }
list-field: {
  x: h(20000)
  y: [x first, x first, x first]
  ok: y = [199990000, 199990000, 199990000]
}
